<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Security on Mornati Blog</title><link>https://blog.mornati.net/tags/security/</link><description>Recent content in Security on Mornati Blog</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en-US</language><copyright>© 2026 Marco Mornati</copyright><lastBuildDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 04:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.mornati.net/tags/security/rss.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Drowning in Email: ai-email-assistant, Rules First, Models Last</title><link>https://blog.mornati.net/drowning-in-email-ai-email-assistant-rules-first-models-last/</link><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 04:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.mornati.net/drowning-in-email-ai-email-assistant-rules-first-models-last/</guid><description>A Gmail triage that costs cents. Deterministic rules handle the routine mail, Claude Haiku looks only at what&amp;rsquo;s left, Claude Sonnet only at what Haiku isn&amp;rsquo;t sure about, and code validates every answer. Requests become Google Tasks with a due date. With a real run on my inbox, a from-zero install with Homebrew, and a few thoughts on letting an AI answer your mail.</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://blog.mornati.net/drowning-in-email-ai-email-assistant-rules-first-models-last/cover.jpg"/></item><item><title>New Week, Another AI Coach: ai-finance-coach</title><link>https://blog.mornati.net/new-week-another-ai-coach-ai-finance-coach/</link><pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.mornati.net/new-week-another-ai-coach-ai-finance-coach/</guid><description>A self-hosted coach for your household&amp;rsquo;s money. PSD2 bank sync through Enable Banking, an encrypted local database, a one-time login link or a passkey, and a language model that only ever receives redacted, pseudonymised, alread